This commit also holds an unrelated change from a parallel session: the
origami layout choice moves from localStorage to sessionStorage (main.js
"case 'layout'" and the boot lines that delete the old origami.layout
key). That change was made in the worktree while this split was in
progress, and the split staged the whole worktree main.js.

Why: a VERTICAL choice saved in localStorage stayed forever and stacked
the panes on a wide screen. Now a forced layout lasts one tab session,
and a new visit starts in AUTO (side by side when wider than tall).

Validation (headless Chrome over CDP, HEAD tree plus that change):
  localStorage origami.layout = 'v', reload at 1920x1200: layout
  "horiz", old key null. At 390x844: layout "vert".
  apply('layout:v') then reload: layout "vert", session "v".
  console errors/warnings: none. node tests.mjs: 132 passed, 0 failed.
